        <p>MILT is beginning. te alarm even I the Tory platy, of which he is the leader. The I news of the preent week gives an sliniiit start- linig • ilibplay of Om imponince and faiinnis if tho cornitry in tho field of foreign ulfaire. In his deal- ings with the Concert of Europe over the Greco- I Turkish ilimpute,with the Freuth Goverment in re- 1 gard to Tome, arid with the Americans on the flu- bring Sea iphoton, Lord SALIM...HY has, a, the represtative if Great Britain, submitted ill the most humiliating manner to the dictation of foreign statimonen.A, we have thideven the T,llOll thnnselve, cannot stand this without protest. Thu " Morning Poet " in a preerunient deo'. the 11101.1t11001.11.1 ill the Loiulio prep of engin:- , ratio Toryism eiarCof the Enron.° Leagurnyet the " Morning Poet " is almost abusive in it. indigo tarn. On On Monday it declared that " shooting materials are supplied by the, nywning's news to enable Engliehmen who taro for their country*. pcsition and hearing in the world to judge of the spirit in which at tho present time the character of tirivet Britain opheld." " When wo find," it adds, " it the satrn, time in- efletual attempts to thnvin. the trout Powers in regard to the settlement of the Etht, con..- .ions without motive to Fran., and 0.11C.11i01111 to Arnerith , in reponse to diplomatic trot- meet without parallel for its want of respect, we can only infer that the reenters cif the Cabinet aro potheseed with a dimht of the ability of the nation in thee of need to felled it. honour or its right.." In. other words, aocerding to tins Tory journaLlintish honour anti rights are thcrifithl by Lord SALIZIICII.y baths.° our "streng Foreign Secretary" is apparently of opinion that thi. country has neither the ability nor the spirit to defend them. A cloth esaininathin of the diplo- matic question. referred to shows that every word of this severe indictment i• thoroughly justified. In the leg drawn out negotiation. for the settlement if th