        <head>POLICE CA9IOI.</head>
        <p>POLICE CA9IOI.</p>
        <p>At the Police Elation, Earlentown, on Saturday farming before Mr. C. B. F. lidrron,llnorge Bell wan Charged with hoing drunk in Crow-lane,Earlentown, and wan fiend 2.n. 01. and coon or 7 days.—On Mon- day at the mania place before Mr. Borton, Bernard Rourke, Patrick Lyons, Ttionane !Unity all collier. of Ilayilock, were charged with being drunk and lighting in Market-street on Saturday. Hawk° woo fined 2d. GI. and torte, and the nth..., si. and nest/. each.—William Hayes. collier nf Ilarlork won charged with bding drunk in Anhton-roail and wry lined 2a dl. and routs.</p>
        <p>_ CHOIR SOCIAL.</p>
        <p>A "social" in connection with the B.S.A.mas held in the Co-operative Hall on Wednesday evening. About 30 eat down to supper at nine o'clock,the provision- ing being superintended by Mrs.Dring. After copper various games were indulged in. The object in view was to bring the scholars closer toge, her and it was • prelinienary to entering upon the P.S.A. work. The party broke up about ten o'clock. Bowtaro, The handicap for Mr. 0. F. Clark's pricer, which wan COMlllenCed Oft Sittllfdfly week W.lbrOught to close on Saturday, There wore 84 entries end after some exciting play the winners were declared to be Talbot, Ist, cane clock, value 30, tPul, omelet, Bottler, value he. ; 3,1 J. Barlow. value</p>
        <p>3s. After the match was ovcr tho prises were pre- minted by Mr. Clark, on the Green, and the thankc of the club were tendered by Mr. Tarituck on behalf of the members, for the prize, no given. [lonize CH•PRI.. E•81.11tITOWN. Special aervicen of thanksgiving for tbe ingather. I ing of the harvent were held in the Baptist Chapel, Barlectown, on Sunday. The chapel was decorated with fruit, flower, and vegetables and the cervices were conducted by the Bev. J. entrain, of Wake- field, formerly of Earlectown, who preached appro- priate diecourees to fairly large congregations. In the afternoon the fe, gentleman hell a childreti'm ervice,when many 4,1111(.8 attended. Special hymns and anthems were cone and the collections which were in aid of tne now schools, amouutea to a little over £lO.</p>
        <p>HAnueetowm Onrngwrit•L Socrery.</p>
        <p>..--.. -.- Out Sunday evening a sacred concert wan given in St. Mary'. Hall, Crow-lane, Harlatown, by the Sarlostown °rehears! Society. This might be terrn-1 ttie opening of the vociety's Reamon, and the manlier in whir, they transited the Varialla items they Auhtnitted Allowed °int during the summer month, they meat have paid diligent fiaLaptioa ii the instruction, of their tutor. Sir. Avhley. There Was not a very largo aBllOllBB, but °woe prevent . . . •</p>
        <p>thoroughly enjoyed what might be called a musical treat.lllThe following wan the programme nub- milted: —March "SiiVPI Tru mow., ' overture "tort and Peasant," cornet into The Lost Chord," Mr. JaineslMteveanon 6 selection from 12:h Masi "Gloria," ming "Thou'rt passing hence," Mr.J,llugb- Sm; selection,l2th Mass "Sanctus" and "Bmedic us" march " Auntria." A collection was made at the close in aid of the society's 1 unit..</p>
