        <p>Mr. 8. Brighouse, county coroner. ,a rli.itada, morn. in 4 held an inunest . tim r nly of Frednrick Blundell, aged twenty•sia years, an engine Iltt-rol 158, Penny's. lane,Haydock, who died cartoon Tuesday morning in the Haydock Cottage Hospital from injurien received • lew hours previously by being run over and terribly man- gled by erre of the cars of the tit. Helena and District Iramway. Company in Park-road, St. flekns. The in. quest was held at the Waggon and Hone. Hotel, flay- dock. Mr. Joseph Massey, solicitor, and Mr. J. P. Cut- tlee,lecretary and manager, appestad for the frame.. Campany. Mr. H. L,. Riley appeared for the Law Acci- dent and Continroancyllociety,with whom the Tramway. Company Mauro again. accident.—Annie Lloyd, a lIUTIP at the hospitel, sail Blundell was admitted into the hospital at twenty ire minutes to twelve on Monday night. He war suffering frnm a compound fracture of the left thigh nnd right leg. The right thigh was dialracato-d, and there were contuainne all over the body. He died before hoe o'clock the neat morning.— Thom. flarri.on, rumildar, of 218, Church-road, Hay. dock, said that on Monday night he was in company with deceased and William Cawley. Ther were all out of work. They walk,' through St. Helene to Merton Rank-road. Ton tram etopped them and he and Cawley got-mn the engine. Cawley knew the driver,.. he had worked for the company aornoi limn ago. Mundell at that time went up into the top anloon of the car. 1t.... the last, or •• theatre " car that they goad,. Blundell Rot off the car and on to the engine at the Primrose Vaults. about halt way down Parir-vind. Thy engine-driver did not remonatrate with them tor getting on. Ile and Cawley stood at the aides of the engine, and deceased stood in the centre at the rear with his back to the door. De- ceased opened the engine door hirneelf, and when he got into the engine lie thought the door had bean dozed properly. When thee merit %front thirty yard,. front Redgate B